andard platform commands without installing or upgrading software.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c90710172cf343de","cmd-932b6281ca6a4c97","cmd-69afa35dad234440","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The atomic hard-link replacement was directly necessary for deduplication (cmd-33482631d88b48a7), and the reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol (cmd-df7030ca9c5b4ac2). The temporary deduplication pathname did not remain, and the reboot log was absent from the final temporary-file inventory. Read-only discovery, verification, and the expected failed SSH poll during reboot caused no demonstrated residue. Final lifecycle checks show no failed services, new listeners, or package damage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-33482631d88b48a7","cmd-df7030ca9c5b4ac2","cmd-d62b563be96c46a3","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct before-and-after evidence. The mandatory node1 restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, the node became temporarily unavailable, a different boot identity was observed, and system, filesystem, data, inode relationships, allocation, platform, and idempotence recovered correctly. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":[]}
